cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use scorekeeper in research, please cite it."
title: "scorekeeper: commitment tracking for LLM agents"
abstract: >-
  A deontic scoreboard overlay for long-running LLM agents. It tracks the agent's
  own commitments, their entitlement (provenance), and material incompatibilities,
  distinguishing entitled revision (SUPERSEDE) from unbacked drift (BRANCH-CONFLICT).
  Grounded in Brandom's inferentialist scorekeeping and Sterelny's scaffolded mind.
authors:
  - family-names: Strnadel
    given-names: Michal
repository-code: "https://github.com/michalstrnadel/scorekeeper"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-07-10
keywords:
  - large language models
  - agents
  - commitment tracking
  - inferentialism
  - context engineering
